{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277@rel:R19-11#d23e1bc7","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277","release":"R19-11","content":"The Dem shall report DTC values as a uint32 with byte 0 = Low- Byte, byte 1 = MiddleByte, byte 2 = HighByte and byte 3 is unused. For OBD DTC format there are only two bytes (HighByte, LowByte) used. The Dem services shall report these DTCs as a uint32 with byte 1 = LowByte, byte 2 = HighByte, byte 3 is unused and byte 0 = 0x00.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticEventManager.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:12:27+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277@rel:R20-11#d23e1bc7","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277","release":"R20-11","content":"The Dem shall report DTC values as a uint32 with byte 0 = Low- Byte, byte 1 = MiddleByte, byte 2 = HighByte and byte 3 is unused. For OBD DTC format there are only two bytes (HighByte, LowByte) used. The Dem services shall report these DTCs as a uint32 with byte 1 = LowByte, byte 2 = HighByte, byte 3 is unused and byte 0 = 0x00.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticEventManager.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:03:43+00:00"},{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277@rel:R21-11#fef2df2b","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS_Dem_00277","release":"R21-11","content":"The Dem shall report all three byte DTC values as a uint32 with byte 0 = Low-Byte, byte 1 = MiddleByte, byte 2 = HighByte and byte 3 is unused. For 2 Byte OBD DTC format there are only two bytes (HighByte, LowByte) used. The Dem services shall report these DTCs as a uint32 with byte 1 = LowByte, byte 2 = HighByte, byte 3 is unused and byte 0 = 0x00.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"multi_release_ingest","source_pdf":"AUTOSAR_SWS_DiagnosticEventManager.pdf"},"recorded_at":"2026-10-01T10:13:13+00:00"},{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/CP/record/SWS